In article <C7z54t.8nM@news.cso.uiuc.edu>, dreamer@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu (Andrew Trapp) writes:
 > I hate nethack.  What's worse is that I'm thoroughly addicted to it.
 > 
 > Thirdly:  The new weight system S U X !!!  If I accumulate any decent amount
 > of possessions, my character moves slower.  When you're surrounded by hordes
 > of rothes or hill orcs (I'm talking beginning levels here), the last thing
 > you want is to find out to your suprise and your character's demise that all
 > of a sudden, they get an _extra_ attack.  A burdened or stressed character
 > now has to have the fast attribute _just_to_break_even_.  T'aint fair, I tell
 > ya.

Moving slower when carrying a lot seems realistic to me.  You have to decide
wether to pick up all those nifty items, or be able to move fast.
You'll never get surprised when the monsters get an extra attack, the
status line clearly states that you are "burdened" or something.  Burdened
isn't that bad, the extra attack occur only now and then.
You don't need to carry everything you find.  Gems and excessive amounts of
gold can be left when you are going down, just remeber to pick it up on
your way back.  You can put it in a box/chest if you don't want the risk
of monsters picking it up.  

 > I also miss being able to easily rob shops blind.  I always ditched my pet
 > on level 1 (preferably locked in a closet).  Now I have to put up with their
 > stealing XP and corpses from me if I want to rob a shop.  I suppose this
 > gripe I could learn to live with, but the game just isn't as fun.  (Tips on
 > robbing shops early in the game would be much appreciated!  ;-)

Stealing isn't that difficult, if you have the proper equipment or
intrinsics.  I haven't tried this, but having a wand of teleportation and a
wand of digging is probably enough.  Teleport out, then dig to avoid the kops.
Robbing was too easy before, just dig a little and then kick,kick,kick...
Never had to pay for anything...

 > On the plus side, I like the addition of more items, monsters, and special
 > levels.  The line-of-sight thingy is also fairly nice, except I don't see
 > why a monster should no longer be visible to me as it steps into a corridor
 > coming towards me.

The corridor is dark.  Use a lamp, and you'll see the monsters when they come
near you.  Using a lamp also lets you find corridor forks faster when
walking around mapping a new level.

